description:
A synthetic benchmark function designed with specific ELA features in mind.

This function combines a skewed sine wave, a product of variables (interaction),
and a power function to sculpt the landscape. It can be written as

f(x) = a * sin(skew * x[0]) + b * (x[0] * x[1]) + c * sum(x[i]**power for i in range(2)) + offset

Where:
- a,b,c are scaling factors;
- skew controls the skewness/frequency of the sine wave;
- power controls the intensity of the power function;
- offset just shifts the function to different ranges.
